      "note": "Tens was already decremented from 4 to 3 to lend a ten to units. When tens itself then needs to borrow from hundreds, the student re-uses the original pre-decrement digit (4+10=14) instead of the already-decremented one (3+10=13) — an off-by-one across a cascading borrow chain."
